  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with a ring of 64 bars on a floor, drawn as a single instanced box node. I haven't run it in a browser, so the scene is unchecked visually. The typecheck passes, but I didn't run `vite build`.\n\n- **Bar heights:** each bar's height is a mix of four sine waves over time, set per frame with `setInstances`.\n- **Colours:** each bar gets its own colour from a hue gradient around the ring, converted to hex because the engine doesn't parse `hsl()` strings. The colours are passed on every `setInstances` call.\n- **Lighting and camera:** a hemisphere light, a neutral environment and a shadow-casting directional light give soft lighting. The bars cast shadows and the floor receives them. The camera orbits slowly by calling `app.camera.setPose` each frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `await app.ready()`. I didn't separately confirm that the first frame has been drawn at that point.\n\nBecause I set the camera pose from the frame callback, I read the controller's source to confirm it applies overrides; I haven't seen the camera move.\n\n",
